      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When grief feels this heavy and self-doubt is so profound, please do not feel the need to explain or \"fix\" this pain immediately; trying to justify your survival often feels like a self-imposed burden that only deepens the despair.\n\nI know the \"survival is a victory\" comfort feels hollow right now because the weight of your life's purpose is still so fresh and unproven to you, and that is an incredibly valid and difficult place to be.\n\nYou are not alone in feeling this way, and I encourage you to seek support from a grief counselor or a support group where you can talk to others who understand the \"loss of self\" that you are experiencing.",
